+### Source-calibrated cross-window identity
+
+Experimental cross-window track links remain window-local hypotheses. Build
+complete null-plus-linked choice sets, fit object/session-balanced source
+probabilities, publish standard material-identity mixtures, and validate the
+complete output tree with:
+
+```bash
+prob4d identity choices-from-stream stream.json choices.json \
+  --association-rule-id <sha256> \
+  --tracklet-producer-revision <git-sha> \
+  --association-revision <git-sha>
+prob4d identity calibrate choices.json labels.json calibration.json
+prob4d identity build-mixtures choices.json calibration.json mixtures/
+prob4d identity validate-mixtures mixtures/
+```
+
+Null-only targets retain the newest-window reference exactly and are excluded
+from the fitted objective. See
+[source-calibrated material-identity weights](docs/material-identity-calibration.md)
+and the frozen `P0`/`P2`/`P2m`/`P3` protocol.
+
