+# Source-calibrated material-identity weights
+
+`prob4d.material_identity_calibration` turns complete cross-window identity
+alternatives into portable source-side probabilities. It does not promote a
+pairwise association score to a posterior probability, rewrite any window-local
+point ID, inspect target outcomes, or decide whether BayesianPhysTwin accepts an
+update.
+
+The output is consumed by the existing
+[`prob4d.material_identity_mixture`](material-identity-marginalization.md)
+contract. Every calibrated choice set contains exactly one null candidate, so a
+missing or rejected cross-window link preserves the newest-window reference
+exactly.
+
+## Why a separate calibration is necessary
+
+`compatibility_score` is a bounded source-side ranking statistic. Its current
+covariance-safe semantics deliberately prevent a candidate from becoming
+mutual-best merely because its covariance is wider. The score is not calibrated
+across candidate-set sizes, window lags, support levels, objects, or acquisition
+sessions.
+
+The calibration layer therefore keeps three operations separate:
+
+1. **candidate generation and pairwise ranking** remain owned by the existing
+   tracklet association code;
+2. **source-side probability calibration** uses only frozen source/calibration
+   identity labels; and
+3. **downstream likelihood and update acceptance** remain owned by
+   BayesianPhysTwin.
+
+## Choice-set construction
+
+Build one canonical choice-set artifact from an append-only hypothesis stream:
+
+```bash
+prob4d identity choices-from-stream \
+  outputs/object-a/material-identities.json \
+  outputs/object-a/identity-choices.json \
+  --association-rule-id <sha256-of-frozen-association-rule> \
+  --tracklet-producer-revision <prob4d-git-sha> \
+  --association-revision <prob4d-git-sha>
+```
+
+Each target-local track receives:
+
+- one null candidate for the unchanged newest-window reference;
+- every evaluated source-linked candidate retained by the stream;
+- the original source `(window_id, track_id)` endpoint;
+- the association result identity and source score; and
+- a fixed source-only feature vector.
+
+The version-1 feature contract contains:
+
+1. null-candidate indicator;
+2. geometric compatibility score;
+3. candidate score margin against the best competing linked candidate;
+4. log effective support;
+5. log weighted RMS in millimetres;
+6. log maximum shared-frame distance in millimetres;
+7. log covariance-normalized RMS diagnostic;
+8. shared-frame count;
+9. pairwise-gate selection indicator;
+10. source-to-target window lag; and
+11. null-only summaries of the best linked score, margin, support, candidate
+    count, and whether any pairwise link was selected.
+
+No target truth, physical innovation, Bayesian posterior responsibility, or
+Causal4D outcome enters these features.
+
+Merge disjoint source/calibration objects or sessions before fitting:
+
+```bash
+prob4d identity merge-choices \
+  outputs/object-a/identity-choices.json \
+  outputs/object-b/identity-choices.json \
+  outputs/object-c/identity-choices.json \
+  --output outputs/calibration/identity-choices.json
+```
+
+All collections must have identical feature, association-rule, producer, and
+association-revision semantics.
+
+## Label artifact
+
+A `prob4d.material-identity-label-set` artifact binds exactly one selected
+candidate to every choice set and assigns every choice set to an independent
+calibration group. The group should normally be a complete physical object,
+acquisition session, or simulation family—not a point, frame, or dense row.
+
+Create it through the public Python helper after source labels have been frozen:
+
+```python
+from prob4d.material_identity_calibration import (
+    create_material_identity_label_set,
+    load_material_identity_choice_sets,
+    write_material_identity_label_set,
+)
+
+choices = load_material_identity_choice_sets("identity-choices.json")
+labels = create_material_identity_label_set(
+    choices,
+    {
+        choice_set_id: (chosen_candidate_id, physical_object_id)
+        for choice_set_id, chosen_candidate_id, physical_object_id in frozen_rows
+    },
+    label_definition="source material-point correspondence v1",
+    group_definition="physical object",
+)
+write_material_identity_label_set(labels, "identity-labels.json")
+```
+
+The label artifact requires `target_outcomes_used=false`, complete one-to-one
+coverage of the choice-set collection, and exact candidate IDs. A label cannot
+silently move to another target track or candidate order.
